{"title": "Sectional Mock #50 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Pipe A and pipe B can fill a tank in 4 hours and 5 hours respectively. There is an outlet pipe C when all three pipes are opened together the tank got filled in 2 (6/7) hours. Find the time taken by C alone to empty the fully filled tank.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; 2 (6/7) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["14 hours", "13 hours", "12 hours", "10 hours"], "options_hi": ["14 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "13 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "10 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let pipe C can empty the tank in x hours.</p><p>Part of tank filled by pipe A in 1 hour = 1/4 </p><p>Part of tank filled by pipe B in 1 hour = 1/5</p><p>Part of the tank filled when all pipes are opened together = 1/(20/7) = 7/20</p><p>According to question,</p><p>1/4 + 1/5  -  1/x = 7/20</p><p>1/4 + 1/5  -  7/20 = 1/x</p><p>(5 + 4  -  7)/20 = 1/x</p><p>2/20 = 1/x</p><p>x = 10 hours </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let pipe C can empty the tank in x hours.</p><p>Part of tank filled by pipe A in 1 hour = 1/4 </p><p>Part of tank filled by pipe B in 1 hour = 1/5</p><p>Part of the tank filled when all pipes are opened together = 1/(20/7) = 7/20</p><p>According to question,</p><p>1/4 + 1/5  -  1/x = 7/20</p><p>1/4 + 1/5  -  7/20 = 1/x</p><p>(5 + 4  -  7)/20 = 1/x</p><p>2/20 = 1/x</p><p>x = 10 hours </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The third proportional of 0.024 and 0.12 is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>0.024 &#2324;&#2352; 0.12 &#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["0.060", "6.000", "0.600", "0.006"], "options_hi": ["0.060", "6.000", "0.600", "0.006"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let third proportional of 0.024 and 0.12 is 'x'.</p><p>Now,</p><p>0.024: 0.12&#8759; 0.12: x</p><p>x = 0.12<sup>2</sup>/0.024</p><p>x = 0.0144/0.024</p><p>x = 0.6</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let third proportional of 0.024 and 0.12 is 'x'.</p><p>Now,</p><p>0.024: 0.12&#8759; 0.12: x</p><p>x = 0.12<sup>2</sup>/0.024</p><p>x = 0.0144/0.024</p><p>x = 0.6</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B started a business with investments of Rs.8400 and Rs.8000 respectively. After 4 months A added Rs.600 to his investment and B withdrew Rs.4000. At the end of one-year partnership, profit earned by A is __% of the profit earned by B.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2352;&#2369;.8400 &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;.8000 &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 4 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; A &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.600 &#2332;&#2379;&#2396;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; B &#2352;&#2369;.4000 &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;, B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; __% &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["220%", "132%", "165%", "225%"], "options_hi": ["220%", "132%", "165%", "225%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>A's initial investment = Rs.8400</p><p>B's initial investment = Rs.8000</p><p>Period of partnership = 1 year = 12 months</p><p>Therefore, profit ratio, A: B = (8400 * 4 + (8400 + 600) * (12  -  4) ): (8000 * 4 + (8000  -  4000) * (12  -  4) )</p><p>= (33600 + 72000) : (32000 + 32000)</p><p>= 105600: 64000</p><p>= 33: 20</p><p>Therefore, percentage = (33/20) * 100 = <b>165%</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A's initial investment = Rs.8400</p><p>B's initial investment = Rs.8000</p><p>Period of partnership = 1 year = 12 months</p><p>Therefore, profit ratio, A: B = (8400 * 4 + (8400 + 600) * (12  -  4) ): (8000 * 4 + (8000  -  4000) * (12  -  4) )</p><p>= (33600 + 72000) : (32000 + 32000)</p><p>= 105600: 64000</p><p>= 33: 20</p><p>Therefore, percentage = (33/20) * 100 = <b>165%</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of given expression  -</p><p><table style=\"border:none\"><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black;padding:5px;text-align:center\"><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">7", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; -</p><p><table style=\"border:none\"><tr><td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black;padding:5px;text-align:center\"><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">7", "options_en": ["-1/2", "2/5", "5/6", "-2/3"], "options_hi": ["-1/2", "2/5", "5/6", "-2/3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=129 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image010.png\"></p><p><img width=75 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image013.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=129 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image010.png\"></p><p><img width=75 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image011.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21382/image013.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ashna secured 65 marks in geography while her scores in history, polity and economics were in the ratio 3: 4: 13 respectively. If her average score in geography, history and economics is 91, then how many marks did she secure in polity?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2358;&#2344;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 65 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;, &#2346;&#2377;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2325;&#2379;&#2344;&#2377;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 3: 4:13 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347;&#2368;, &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2325;&#2379;&#2344;&#2377;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 91 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2377;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["48", "52", "56", "44"], "options_hi": ["48", "52", "56", "44"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the marks secured by Ashna in history, polity and economics be 3a, 4a and 13a respectively.</p><p>Marks secured by Ashna in geography = 65</p><p>Now, 3 * 91 = 3a + 13a + 65</p><p>273 = 16a + 65</p><p>16a = 208</p><p>a = 13</p><p>Therefore, marks secured by Ashna in polity = 4a = 4 * 13 = <b>52</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the marks secured by Ashna in history, polity and economics be 3a, 4a and 13a respectively.</p><p>Marks secured by Ashna in geography = 65</p><p>Now, 3 * 91 = 3a + 13a + 65</p><p>273 = 16a + 65</p><p>16a = 208</p><p>a = 13</p><p>Therefore, marks secured by Ashna in polity = 4a = 4 * 13 = <b>52</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value closest to:</p><p>&radic;(8 + 2&radic;15) - &radic;(14 + 6&radic;5)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p>&radic;(8 + 2&radic;15) - &radic;(14 + 6&radic;5)</p>", "options_en": ["-0.8", "-2.4", "-1.8", "-1.2"], "options_hi": ["-0.8", "-2.4", "-1.8", "-1.2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=153 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image065.png\"></p><p><img width=235 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=355 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=177 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=121 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image069.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image070.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image071.png\"></p><p><img width=64 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image072.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=153 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image065.png\"></p><p><img width=235 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=355 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=177 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=121 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image069.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image070.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image071.png\"></p><p><img width=64 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15407/image072.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A can fill a tank in 30 hours and pipe B can fill the same tank in 45 hours. If pipe C can empty the full tank in 25 hours, then find the time taken by all three pipes together to fill 70% of the tank. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 30 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 45 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 25 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; 70% &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["35 hours", "45 hours", "32 hours", "42 hours"], "options_hi": ["35 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "45 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "32 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "42 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The capacity of tank = L.C.M of 25, 45, and 30 = 450</p><p>Efficiency = The capacity of a tank/ time taken</p><p>Efficiency of A = 450/30 = 15</p><p>Efficiency of B = 450/45 = 10</p><p>Efficiency of C = 450/25 = 18</p><p>The total efficiency of A, B, and C = (15 + 10  -  18) = 7</p><p>Hence, the required time = (450 * 70/100)/7 = 45 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The capacity of tank = L.C.M of 25, 45, and 30 = 450</p><p>Efficiency = The capacity of a tank/ time taken</p><p>Efficiency of A = 450/30 = 15</p><p>Efficiency of B = 450/45 = 10</p><p>Efficiency of C = 450/25 = 18</p><p>The total efficiency of A, B, and C = (15 + 10  -  18) = 7</p><p>Hence, the required time = (450 * 70/100)/7 = 45 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following pie chart shows the percentage distribution of the expenditure incurred in publishing a book. Study the pie chart and answer the question that follows.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27249/image024.png\"></p><p>If the expenditure on royalty in publishing certain number of books be Rs. 43500, then what is the combined expenditure (in Rs.) on transportation, binding and printing?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27249/image024.png\"></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2377;&#2351;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; 43500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2361;&#2344;, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2369;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["1,97,900", "1,79,400", "1,79,900", "1,47,900"], "options_hi": ["1,97,900", "1,79,400", "1,79,900", "1,47,900"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total expenditure = (43,500 / 15)  X  100 = &#8377;2,90,000</p><p>Percentage on transportation, binding, and printing= 10% + 16% + 25%=51%</p><p>So expenditure= 51% of 290000=147900.</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total expenditure = (43,500 / 15)  X  100 = &#8377;2,90,000</p><p>Percentage on transportation, binding, and printing= 10% + 16% + 25%=51%</p><p>So expenditure= 51% of 290000=147900.</p><p>Option (d) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A metallic ball of radius 2.4 cm is melted and completely made into a wire of length 4.8 cm. The radius of the wire will be:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2.4 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2327;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 4.8 cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;:</p>", "options_en": ["4&radic;3/5 cm", "4&radic;6 cm", "4&radic;6/5 cm", "4&radic;3 cm"], "options_hi": ["4&radic;3/5 cm", "4&radic;6 cm", "4&radic;6/5 cm", "4&radic;3 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>As wire is made by melting the sphere, volume of sphere = volume of wire</p><p>(4/3) * &pi; * 2.4 * 2.4 * 2.4 = &pi; * r<sup>2</sup> * 4.8</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 96/25</p><p>r = 4&radic;6/5 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As wire is made by melting the sphere, volume of sphere = volume of wire</p><p>(4/3) * &pi; * 2.4 * 2.4 * 2.4 = &pi; * r<sup>2</sup> * 4.8</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 96/25</p><p>r = 4&radic;6/5 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A certain sum invested for 3 years at a rate of simple interest of 5% per annum gives Rs.2400 as interest. What will be the extra interest received if the interest is compounded annually:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>5% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 2400 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.132", "Rs.112", "Rs.152", "Rs.122"], "options_hi": ["132", "&#2352;&#2369;.112", "152", "&#2352;&#2369;.122"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=255 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20434/image020.png\"></p><p>Hence the Sum = Rs.16000</p><p><img width=501 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20434/image021.png\"></p><p>Hence, the extra interest received if the interest is compounded annually = 2522  -  2400 = <b>Rs.122</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=255 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20434/image020.png\"></p><p>Hence the Sum = Rs.16000</p><p><img width=501 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20434/image021.png\"></p><p>Hence, the extra interest received if the interest is compounded annually = 2522  -  2400 = <b>Rs.122</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum of two numbers is 45 and their H.C.F is 5. Find the possible number of pairs.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 45 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; 5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>H.C.F= 5</p><p>x : y</p><p>5x + 5y= 45</p><p>x + y = 9</p><p>So, the possible pairs are: (1,8); (2,7) and (4,5)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>H.C.F= 5</p><p>x : y</p><p>5x + 5y= 45</p><p>x + y = 9</p><p>So, the possible pairs are: (1,8); (2,7) and (4,5)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A thief running at 18 kmph, is chased by a policeman whose speed is 20 kmph. If the thief is 125 m ahead of the policeman, the time required for the policeman to catch the thief will be:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>18 kmph &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2379;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 20 kmph &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2330;&#2379;&#2352;, &#2346;&#2369;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; 125 m &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2330;&#2379;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["3 min 25 sec", "3 min 40 sec", "3 min 30 sec", "3 min 45 sec"], "options_hi": ["3 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; 25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "3 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; 40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "3 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; 30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "3 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; 45 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Distance between thief and policeman = 125 m</p><p>Relative speed of policeman with respect to thief = 20 - 18 = 2 kmph = 2 * 5/18 m/sec = 5/9 m/sec</p><p>Required time = 125 * 9/5 = 225 sec = 3 min 45 sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance between thief and policeman = 125 m</p><p>Relative speed of policeman with respect to thief = 20 - 18 = 2 kmph = 2 * 5/18 m/sec = 5/9 m/sec</p><p>Required time = 125 * 9/5 = 225 sec = 3 min 45 sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If SinA =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; SinA = <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a", "options_en": ["2a<sup>2</sup>/b<sup>2</sup>", "2a/b", "2a<sup>2</sup>/b", "2a/b<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["2a<sup>2</sup>/b<sup>2</sup>", "2a/b", "2a<sup>2</sup>/b", "2a/b<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>SinA = a/b, then CosA = &radic;[1  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>A] = &radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)/b</p><p>Value of Sin2A/&radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; 2SinACosA/&radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; [2 * (a/b) * (&radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)/b)]/ &radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; 2a/b<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>SinA = a/b, then CosA = &radic;[1  -  Sin<sup>2</sup>A] = &radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)/b</p><p>Value of Sin2A/&radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; 2SinACosA/&radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; [2 * (a/b) * (&radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)/b)]/ &radic;(b<sup>2</sup>  -  a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>=&gt; 2a/b<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a triangle ABC, AB = 33 cm, AC = 56 cm, and BC = 65 cm. From vertex A, a median AD is drawn that meets BC at point D. If G is the point on AD that denotes centroid, then find the length of AG.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, AB = 33 cm, AC = 56 cm &#2324;&#2352; BC = 65 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; A &#2360;&#2375;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; AD &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; BC &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; D &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AD &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; G &#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; AG &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["21.66 cm", "23.33 cm", "19.22 cm", "24.11 cm"], "options_hi": ["21.66 cm", "23.33 cm", "19.22 cm", "24.11 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Sides of the triangle are 33 cm, 56 cm, and 65 cm.</p><p>We know that (33, 56, 65) is a Pythagorean triplet.</p><p>Therefore, ABC is a right triangle.</p><p>Median (AD) = Hypotenuse/2 = 65/2 cm</p><p>We know that centroid divides the median in the ratio of 2: 1.</p><p>So, AG = AD * 2/3 = (65/2) * (2/3) = 21.66 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sides of the triangle are 33 cm, 56 cm, and 65 cm.</p><p>We know that (33, 56, 65) is a Pythagorean triplet.</p><p>Therefore, ABC is a right triangle.</p><p>Median (AD) = Hypotenuse/2 = 65/2 cm</p><p>We know that centroid divides the median in the ratio of 2: 1.</p><p>So, AG = AD * 2/3 = (65/2) * (2/3) = 21.66 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the least number which when decreased by 11 is divisible by 19, 24, 18, 32?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 11 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361; 19, 24, 18 &#2324;&#2352; 32 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["5472", "5483", "5461", "5450"], "options_hi": ["5472", "5483", "5461", "5450"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>L.C.M of 19, 24, 18 and 32 = 5472</p><p>The required number = 5472 + 11 = 5483</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>L.C.M of 19, 24, 18 and 32 = 5472</p><p>The required number = 5472 + 11 = 5483</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup>, then which option is correct?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1/x  -  2/y  -  2/z = 0", "1/x + 2/y + 1/z = 0", "2/x + 1/y  -  1/z = 0", "1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0"], "options_hi": ["1/x  -  2/y  -  2/z = 0", "1/x + 2/y + 1/z = 0", "2/x + 1/y  -  1/z = 0", "1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup></p><p>Let 4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup> = k</p><p>4 = k<sup>1/x</sup>............(i)</p><p>7 = k<sup>1/y</sup>............(ii)</p><p>28 = k<sup>-1/z</sup>...........(iii)</p><p>4 * 7 = 28</p><p>k<sup>1/x</sup> * k<sup>1/y</sup> = k<sup>-1/z</sup>............using eq(i), (ii) and (iii)</p><p>k<sup>1/x</sup> <sup>+ 1/y</sup> = k<sup>-1/z</sup></p><p>1/x + 1/y = -1/z</p><p>1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup></p><p>Let 4<sup>x</sup> = 7<sup>y</sup> = 28<sup>-z</sup> = k</p><p>4 = k<sup>1/x</sup>............(i)</p><p>7 = k<sup>1/y</sup>............(ii)</p><p>28 = k<sup>-1/z</sup>...........(iii)</p><p>4 * 7 = 28</p><p>k<sup>1/x</sup> * k<sup>1/y</sup> = k<sup>-1/z</sup>............using eq(i), (ii) and (iii)</p><p>k<sup>1/x</sup> <sup>+ 1/y</sup> = k<sup>-1/z</sup></p><p>1/x + 1/y = -1/z</p><p>1/x + 1/y + 1/z = 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A alone can do work in 48 days and ratio of efficiency of A to B is 4: 3. They together start working on a work and work for 6 days after another person C joins them and together they finish the remaining work in 10 more days. If they undertook to do the work for Rs.5250, then what is the share of B?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; 48 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; A &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2358;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4:3 &#2361;&#2376;| &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; C &#2313;&#2344;&#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2369;&#2396;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; 10 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 5250 &#2352;&#2369; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2366;&#2351;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.1050", "Rs.1312.5", "Rs.1120.5", "Rs.1200"], "options_hi": ["1050 &#2352;&#2369;", "1312.5 &#2352;&#2369;", "1120.5 &#2352;&#2369;", "1200 &#2352;&#2369;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Time taken by A alone to do the work = 48 days</p><p>Time taken by B alone to do the work = 48 * (4/3) = 64 days</p><p>Total days for which A and B work = 6 + 10 = 16 days</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>(16/48) + (16/64) + (10/C) = 1</p><p>(10/C) = 1  -  (1/3)  -  (1/4)</p><p>(10/C) = (5/12)</p><p>C = 24 days</p><p>Part of work done by A = (16/48) = 1/3</p><p>Part of work done by B = (16/64) = 1/4</p><p>Part of work done by C = (10/24) = 5/12</p><p>Ratio of their work done = (1/3): (1/4): (5/12) = 4: 3: 5</p><p>Share of B = 5250 * (3/12) = Rs.1312.5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Time taken by A alone to do the work = 48 days</p><p>Time taken by B alone to do the work = 48 * (4/3) = 64 days</p><p>Total days for which A and B work = 6 + 10 = 16 days</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>(16/48) + (16/64) + (10/C) = 1</p><p>(10/C) = 1  -  (1/3)  -  (1/4)</p><p>(10/C) = (5/12)</p><p>C = 24 days</p><p>Part of work done by A = (16/48) = 1/3</p><p>Part of work done by B = (16/64) = 1/4</p><p>Part of work done by C = (10/24) = 5/12</p><p>Ratio of their work done = (1/3): (1/4): (5/12) = 4: 3: 5</p><p>Share of B = 5250 * (3/12) = Rs.1312.5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vessel contains a mixture of salt and water in the ratio of 2: 3. If 12 litre of water is vaporized from the mixture, then the quantity of salt and water becomes equal. Find the initial quantity of the mixture.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 2 : 3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2350;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375; 12 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2359;&#2381;&#2346;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2350;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["24 litre", "36 litre", "48 litre", "60 litre"], "options_hi": ["24 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "36 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "48 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "60 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=529 height=68 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23256/image003.png\" ></p><p>The initial quantity of the mixture = 12 * 5 = 60 litre</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=529 height=68 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23256/image003.png\" ></p><p>The initial quantity of the mixture = 12 * 5 = 60 litre</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If <img width=75 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image036.png\">, then the value of n is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; <img width=75 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image036.png\">, &#2340;&#2379; n &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["7/5", "5/3", "2/5", "1/5"], "options_hi": ["7/5", "5/3", "2/5", "1/5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=75 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=80 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=103 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=44 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image041.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=75 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=80 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=103 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=44 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image041.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin15&deg;cos75&deg; + sec52&deg;sin38&deg; + sin75&deg;cos15&deg;", "q_hi": "<p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">sin15&deg;cos75&deg; + sec52&deg;sin38&deg; + sin75&deg;cos15&deg;", "options_en": ["1", "2", "0", "1/2"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "0", "1/2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=285 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image050.png\"></p><p><img width=421 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image051.png\"></p><p><img width=243 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image052.png\"></p><p><img width=44 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image053.png\"></p><p><img width=25 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image054.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=285 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image050.png\"></p><p><img width=421 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image051.png\"></p><p><img width=243 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image052.png\"></p><p><img width=44 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image053.png\"></p><p><img width=25 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19189/image054.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average of five consecutive even numbers is 92. What is the largest of these numbers?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 92 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["96", "98", "92", "94"], "options_hi": ["96", "98", "92", "94"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the numbers be 'X', 'X + 2', 'X + 4', 'X + 6', and 'X + 8'.</p><p>X + X + 2 + X + 4 + X + 6 + X + 8 = 92 * 5</p><p>5X + 20 = 460</p><p>5X = 440</p><p>X = 88</p><p>Hence, the required number 88 + 8 = 96</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the numbers be 'X', 'X + 2', 'X + 4', 'X + 6', and 'X + 8'.</p><p>X + X + 2 + X + 4 + X + 6 + X + 8 = 92 * 5</p><p>5X + 20 = 460</p><p>5X = 440</p><p>X = 88</p><p>Hence, the required number 88 + 8 = 96</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B borrowed Rs.20910 each from a shopkeeper. A and B returned amount in two equal installments at 4% and 5% rate of simple interest. What is the total interest received by shopkeeper?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 20910 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 4% &#2324;&#2352; 5% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2354;&#2380;&#2335;&#2366;&#2312;&#2404; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.2450", "Rs.2380", "Rs.2760", "Rs.2530"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.2450", "&#2352;&#2369;.2380", "&#2352;&#2369;.2760", "&#2352;&#2369;.2530"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>For A:</p><p>Let each installment = Rs. a</p><p>Then, 20910 x (1 + 4 x 2/100) = a x (1 + 4 x 1/100) + a</p><p>a = 11070</p><p>For B:</p><p>Let each installment = Rs. b</p><p>Then, 20910 x (1 + 5 x 2/100) = b x (1 + 5 x 1/100) + b</p><p>b = 11220</p><p>Then, total interest received by shopkeeper = 2a + 2b  -  2 x 20910</p><p>= 2 x 11070 + 2 x 11220  -  2 x 20910</p><p>= <b>Rs.2760</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For A:</p><p>Let each installment = Rs. a</p><p>Then, 20910 x (1 + 4 x 2/100) = a x (1 + 4 x 1/100) + a</p><p>a = 11070</p><p>For B:</p><p>Let each installment = Rs. b</p><p>Then, 20910 x (1 + 5 x 2/100) = b x (1 + 5 x 1/100) + b</p><p>b = 11220</p><p>Then, total interest received by shopkeeper = 2a + 2b  -  2 x 20910</p><p>= 2 x 11070 + 2 x 11220  -  2 x 20910</p><p>= <b>Rs.2760</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of 312  -  (224 x 108 &div; 252  -  250 &div; 72 x 36 &div; 5)  -  6 x (456  -  302 + 77  -  193)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>312 - (224 x 108 &div; 252 - 250 &div; 72 x 36 &div; 5) - 6 x (456 - 302 + 77 - 193) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12", "13", "15", "14"], "options_hi": ["12", "13", "15", "14"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>= 312  -  (224 x 108 &div; 252  -  250 &div; 72 x 36 &div; 5)  -  6 x (456  -  302 + 77  -  193)</p><p>= 312  -  (96  -  25)  -  6 x 38</p><p>= <b>13</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>= 312  -  (224 x 108 &div; 252  -  250 &div; 72 x 36 &div; 5)  -  6 x (456  -  302 + 77  -  193)</p><p>= 312  -  (96  -  25)  -  6 x 38</p><p>= <b>13</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>If X<sup>4</sup> + X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>4</sup> = 432 and X<sup>2</sup>  -  XY + Y<sup>2</sup> = 18, then find the value of X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> is. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X<sup>4</sup> + X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>4</sup> = 432 &#2324;&#2352; X<sup>2</sup> - XY + Y<sup>2</sup> = 18, &#2340;&#2379; X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["21", "15", "18", "27"], "options_hi": ["21", "15", "18", "27"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  XY + Y<sup>2</sup> = 18 .... (i)</p><p>As we know, </p><p>(X<sup>2</sup>  -  XY + Y<sup>2</sup>) (X<sup>2</sup> + XY + Y<sup>2</sup>) = X<sup>4</sup> + X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>4</sup></p><p>18 * (X<sup>2</sup> + XY + Y<sup>2)</sup> = 432 </p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + XY + Y<sup>2</sup> = 24 .... (ii)</p><p>Add (i) and (ii)</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = (18 + 24)/2 = 21 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>X<sup>2</sup>  -  XY + Y<sup>2</sup> = 18 .... (i)</p><p>As we know, </p><p>(X<sup>2</sup>  -  XY + Y<sup>2</sup>) (X<sup>2</sup> + XY + Y<sup>2</sup>) = X<sup>4</sup> + X<sup>2</sup>Y<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>4</sup></p><p>18 * (X<sup>2</sup> + XY + Y<sup>2)</sup> = 432 </p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + XY + Y<sup>2</sup> = 24 .... (ii)</p><p>Add (i) and (ii)</p><p>X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = (18 + 24)/2 = 21 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>One laddoo with a radius of 5 cm belongs to a shopkeeper. How many laddoos of radius 2.5 cm may be created from the same one laddoo?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2370; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2354;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2370; &#2360;&#2375; 2.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2337;&#2381;&#2337;&#2370; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "6", "4", "8"], "options_hi": ["2", "6", "4", "8"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Radius of large laddoo = 5 cm</p><p>Volume of large laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup></p><p>Radius of small laddoo = 2.5 cm</p><p>Volume of small laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * (2.5)<sup>3</sup></p><p>Number of small laddoos = [4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup>]/[ 4/3 &#960; * 2.5<sup>3</sup>] = (5/2.5)<sup>3</sup> = 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius of large laddoo = 5 cm</p><p>Volume of large laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup></p><p>Radius of small laddoo = 2.5 cm</p><p>Volume of small laddoo = 4/3 &#960; * (2.5)<sup>3</sup></p><p>Number of small laddoos = [4/3 &#960; * 5<sup>3</sup>]/[ 4/3 &#960; * 2.5<sup>3</sup>] = (5/2.5)<sup>3</sup> = 8</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}]}